        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0d2578dd-6a37-58fc-8d5b-a312e8c8fb5b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Rhys-Davies, Timothy Dalton, Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, Salli Richardson, Jamie Foxx\n- Films and TV series: The Untouchables, Shōgun, Sliders, Robin of Sherwood, The Living Daylights, I, Claudius, The Great White Hype, James Bond film series\n- Roles: Agent Michael Malone, Pilot Vasco Rodrigues, Professor Maximillian Arturo, King Richard I, General Leonid Pushkin, Macro, James Bond\n\nFacts:\n- John Rhys-Davies played Macro in the television series \"I, Claudius\".\n- John Rhys-Davies played Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the mini-series \"Shōgun\".\n- John Rhys-Davies played King Richard I in \"Robin of Sherwood\".\n- In 1987, \"The Living Daylights\" was released as the fifteenth film in the James Bond film series.\n- In 1987, Timothy Dalton became the first actor to portray James Bond in \"The Living Daylights\".\n- John Rhys-Davies played General Leonid Pushkin in the James Bond film \"The Living Daylights\".\n- In 1993, John Rhys-Davies played Agent Michael Malone in the remake of the 1950s television series \"The Untouchables\".\n- John Rhys-Davies played Professor Maximillian Arturo in \"Sliders\".\n- \"The Great White Hype\" stars Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, John Rhys-Davies, Salli Richardson, and Jamie Foxx.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fbef7796-a860-5284-a0da-23fef0a0f64e",
        "text": "Page: John Rhys-Davies. Sentence: He also played Agent Michael Malone in the 1993 remake of the 1950s television series \"The Untouchables\", Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the mini-series \"Shōgun\", Professor Maximillian Arturo in \"Sliders\", King Richard I in \"Robin of Sherwood\", General Leonid Pushkin in the James Bond film \"The Living Daylights\", and Macro in \"I, Claudius\".\nPage: The Living Daylights. Sentence: The Living Daylights (1987) is the fifteenth entry in the \"James Bond\" film series and the first to star Timothy Dalton as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.\nPage: The Great White Hype. Sentence: It stars Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, John Rhys-Davies, Salli Richardson and Jamie Foxx.",
